So I rolled an Orcish Rogue, playing on the devnull tournament, and
actually did pretty well with her. An apparent dagger shortage lead me
to /twoweapon Grimtooth and a long sword, which was working
surprisingly well. After almost getting stuck on the Quest I managed to
blank a cursed scroll and write a c?oT using my magic marker.. I had a
lot of fun with this Quest, it was one of the more memorable ones for
sure.

Anyway my problems began when I got down to Medusa - it was the variant
with the Titan, who raped my last character to encounter him (by
surrounding me with baddies). Well, this time the Titan wasn't too much
of a bother.. but there were a *lot* of gremlins on the level already
by the time I realized I shouldn't have let them start multiplying. By
the time I stepped on a magic trap and got 4 gremlin pets, there were
already probably 12 in the room, and then, to see what would happen if
I just let my pet gremlins stay near the water, I let them multiply a
bit more. Neat, now I have about 30 pet gremlins. I left to go do some
sacrificing and when I came back, many of the gremlins were hostile.
So, I killed those that I could, knowing I'd take a big hit to
alignment, then dug down and came back up to deal with Medusa (I had no
means of levitation). Well, there were no levboots in the Perseus
statue, so I figured I was pretty much ready to go down to the Castle
anyway - I wanted to go kill Moloch's priest as I still lacked MR at
this point. I thought *that* would be my death - but read on..

Exploring the first maze level below Medusa, dlvl 22, I was just
casually strolling along when..

You fall into a pit of iron spikes! The spikes were poisoned! -more-
The poison was deadly...
DYWYPI?

I stared in disbelief for a few seconds - I mean, I'm an ORC. How can I
be affected by measly poison? Then I remembered all those damn
gremlins, and yeah, I had been playing all day so it was already
nighttime. So I accepted the death. However, I must say I find it
unfair, and not in a "RNG hates me!" kind of way, but in a "programming
oversight" kind of way. Here's my reasoning: Poison resistance, like
sleep resistance for elves, is a racial characteristic, as opposed to
about 12 other intrinsics the gremlin *could* have stolen that were
gained along the way - from eating corpses, from my god, or from my
class (stealth). Even class-related intrinsics should be stealable
because they represent "learned" skills, or so I always thought - but a
gremlin should not be able to steal your racial intrinsic (unless
you're maybe polymorphed into something else).

I know, I know, I'm being terribly whiny and splitting hairs here, but
come on.. this is the epitomy of an *annoying* death - lord knows I've
had my share of YASD's, so when I get far, exercising all sorts of
caution, and then die on a bloody poisoned spike, it's pretty
frustrating.
And I don't think it's too imbalancing to make orc's poison resistance
an unsteable intrinsic, in the next version of Nethack to come out.



